From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Buldygin <froooks@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] video: rockchip: mpp: reject non-contiguous buffers on
 no-iommu devices

On SoCs without an IOMMU (e.g. rv1106/rv1103) mpp_dma_import_fd() only
programs the first scatter-gather segment address into the hardware
(buffer->iova = sg_dma_address(sgt->sgl)).  If user space imports a buffer
that is not a single physically contiguous run - for example one allocated
from the non-contiguous dma-heap "system" pool - the codec DMA walks off
the end of the first segment into unrelated or unmapped DRAM.  In the best
case this raises a VEPU write-bus error and a device reset; in the worst
case it silently corrupts whatever memory the stray access lands on, which
on a no-iommu system is unprotected.

Detect the condition (iommu_info is NULL on a no-iommu device and the first
segment does not cover the whole dma-buf) and fail the import with a clear
error instead of trusting a truncated address.  Buffers destined for the
hardware on such SoCs must be allocated from the CMA dma-heap.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_iommu.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_iommu.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_iommu.c
index ff93d7f75e6c..ee9f83f7614b 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_iommu.c
@@ -253,6 +253,22 @@ struct mpp_dma_buffer *mpp_dma_import_fd(struct mpp_iommu_info *iommu_info,
 		mpp_err("dma_buf_map_attachment fd %d failed(%d)\n", fd, ret);
 		goto fail_map;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * On a device with no IOMMU only the first scatter-gather segment
+	 * address is programmed into the hardware, so a buffer that is not a
+	 * single physically contiguous run would make the codec DMA overrun
+	 * into unrelated/unmapped DRAM.  Reject it here with a clear message
+	 * instead of silently corrupting memory (userspace must allocate such
+	 * buffers from the CMA dma-heap).
+	 */
+	if (!iommu_info && sg_dma_len(sgt->sgl) < dmabuf->size) {
+		dev_err(dma->dev,
+			"fd %d: non-contiguous buffer on no-iommu device (first segment %u < size %zu); allocate from the CMA dma-heap\n",
+			fd, sg_dma_len(sgt->sgl), dmabuf->size);
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+		dma_buf_unmap_attachment(attach, sgt, buffer->dir);
+		goto fail_map;
+	}
 	buffer->iova = sg_dma_address(sgt->sgl);
 	buffer->size = sg_dma_len(sgt->sgl);
 	buffer->attach = attach;
-- 
2.53.0
